 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "rtl-design-creation",
  "visit": 6,
  "text": "The RTL does not fix these FDA-CON-8 failures, so they are still open. I restored `p2_bram_rom_top.sv` to its original text, and no RTL file has changed.\n\nThe spec declares `core.rst`, `core.h_we`, `core.h_re`, `core.h_addr`, `core.h_wdata`, `core.h_rdata` and `core.led` as ports of the core module. The top-level ports are `clk`, `led` and `sfp_tx_disable`. The core already has all of its ports, and the top already drives them from `jtag_bus`.\n\nI tried adding `h_we`, `h_re`, `h_addr`, `h_wdata` and `h_rdata` as ports on the top. Lint still reported every one of the seven `core.*` names missing, so the check is matching the literal `core.` names, which no top port can have. The extra ports would also have been top-level pins with no board pin and no I/O timing, so I took them out again.\n\nThat leaves two options:\n- **Fix the check:** make FDA-CON-8 skip `core.`-prefixed spec ports, or look them up in `p2_bram_rom_core` instead of the top.\n- **Fix the spec:** move the `core.*` entries out of the spec's `ports:` list, for example into a separate core-port list. That is a spec change, outside this stage.\n\nThe earlier lint output also showed two Verilator warnings in `data/jtag_bus.sv` (unused `tdo` and `cmd_s[45]`). That file must stay byte-identical, so I left it alone.\n\nDONE"
 },
